PT – RLP: New SAP Instance Setup Steps

1. Create SAP Audit Metadata File
   •   Create a new file: sap_auditmetadata.csv containing all SAP table details for PT-RLP.
   •   Location:
awsrepo/src/glue_code/sapptr1p/sap_auditmetadata/

⸻

2. Create New AWS Step Function JSON
   •   File name: step_func_orchestrate_sapptrlp.json
   •   Place it in the new instance folder:
awsrepo/src/step_function/dev/sapptrlp/

⸻

3. Update Terraform Variables for Step Function Deployment
   •   Update terraform.tfvars to include the new variable state_machine10.
   •   Terraform will deploy this new Step Function to AWS.
   •   Path:
awsrepo/iac/us-east-2/dev/stepfunction/

⸻

4. Create Lambda Python Codes
Create the following Lambda scripts under:
src/lambda_code/sapptrlp/
   •   lambda_insert.py
   •   lambda_call_extracts.py
   •   lambda_check_status_extracts.py
   •   trigger_glueworkflow.py

Note:
The trigger_glueworkflow.py script calls the following Glue Workflow:
GLUE_WORKFLOW_NAME = "DAW-tennecosapptrlp-care-proc-workflow"

⸻

5. Update Lambda Terraform Variables
   •   In terraform.tfvars, add new variables (e.g., Lambda361, Lambda362, …)
   •   Define the SAP tables under:
EXTRACTNAMES = "BSEG, ...".
   •   These Lambda functions will be triggered by the Step Function JSON created earlier.
   •   Folder Path:
awsrepo/iac/us-east-2/dev/lambda/

⸻

6. Define Glue Jobs for S3 → GL Load
   •   Create a new terraform.tfvars file defining all Glue jobs for S3 to GL data movement.
   •   Folder Path:
awsrepo/iac/us-east-2/dev/glue/sapptrlp/

⸻

7. Create Glue Workflow Terraform File
   •   Create glue-workflow-ingestion.tf to orchestrate dependencies among the Glue jobs defined in Step 6.
   •   This ensures sequential job execution (S3 → GL).
   •   Folder Path:
awsrepo/iac/us-east-2/prod/glue/sapptrlp/